From: RICE0707 <master.end.9377@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:35:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf: Optimize goal selector

Original license: GPL-3.0-only
Original project: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

Co-authored-by: hayanesuru <hayanesuru@outlook.jp>

Keep the available goals in an array sorted by priority and iterate it directly instead of walking a linked hash set, and decide whether a goal may take its flags by comparing against a small per-flag priority table instead of looking each flag up in the locked map.

Differences from the Leaf version: goals of equal priority keep their insertion order, duplicates are still detected with WrappedGoal.equals as the original set did, and the loops tolerate the goal set being changed while a tick is running.

